**D3. The API switch (B417-1).** Replace `configuration.GetValue<bool>("Auth:UatOpen:Enabled")` with a read of the RAW string and an ordinal comparison, keeping today's outcome for every other value. **The table (REQUIRED; first MEASURE today's outcome of every row at `wt-b418-base` with a probe of `UatOpenAuthentication.Read` under in-memory configuration, label `uat`, a `-uat-` site, a good key and seed owner, and record it; the rows below are the intended outcome):**
| value of `Auth:UatOpen:Enabled` | intended outcome |
|---|---|
| absent (null) | off (`Read` returns null) |
| exactly `false` | off |
| exactly `true` | open (every other lock decides, as today) |
| `True`, `TRUE`, `tRuE`, `" true"`, `"true "`, `"true\t"`, `"true\n"`, `" true "` | **refuse to start** (a `Refuse(...)` that names the setting, never the value; today these open or parse as on) |
| `False`, `FALSE`, `" false"`, `""`, `on`, `ON`, `on `, `1`, `yes`, `no`, `0` | **unchanged from today's measured outcome** (B417 measured `""`, `on`, `on `, `ON`, `1`, `yes` as a binder start-up failure: it must still refuse to start, and `False`/`FALSE` must keep behaving as the base probe shows; if the probe shows a cell different from B417's, say so in Corrections) |
Rationale to record: a padded or case-varied "true" in a template that meant "on" is a mistake the host should say out loud, not run open; refusing is the same direction the label (`"uat "`) and the other padded switches already take (B417 "d3", RELAYED). Do not trim or case-fold anything anywhere. **REQUIRED rows (RED at base, in `UatOpenTests.cs`):** one labelled row per cell of the table (theory rows are fine, one InlineData per cell, names carrying the value); a **host-start row** through the real host for `"true "` (refuses to start; today starts open: B417 MEASURED, RELAYED) and for exact `true` (starts); the existing `Read_with_every_lock_holding_returns_the_settings` stays green unedited. **Mutants:** m3-a revert to `GetValue<bool>`; m3-b `string.Equals(..., OrdinalIgnoreCase)`; m3-c compare after `Trim()`; m3-d exact `true` no longer opens (the control row red). Each must turn a named row RED. Messages carry no value (B417-5: the old binder message printed the value; the new refusal must not).
